13. Patients with deep venous thrombosis, pulmonary embolism or any other serious thromboembolism within 3 months prior to the first dose (implantable venous access-port, catheter-related thrombosis or superficial venous thrombosis is not considered as "serious" thromboembolism);
14. The presence of drug abuse and medical, psychological, or social conditions that do not permit compliance with the protocol or will not be available for protocol-required study visits or procedures.

