Inclusion Criteria:

1. Healthy male or female participants aged between 18 and 50 years (including 18 and 50 years) (the ratio of male/female participants to all is required to be no less than 1/3 in the groups with the dose of 200mg, 400mg and 800mg);
2. Male weight in the range of 50 kg(inclusive) to 90kg, female weight in the range of 45 kg(inclusive) to 90 kg, body mass index (BMI= weight/height square (kg/㎡)) :19.0≤BMI \ ULN, or lipase or amylase \>ULN at screening/baseline visit;
20. Serum creatinine \>ULN at screening/baseline visit;
21. During the screening period, infectious diseases are screened for any positive of hepatitis B surface antigen (HBsAg), hepatitis B core antibody (HBcAb), hepatitis C antibody (anti-HCV), human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) antibody and syphilis antibody.
22. Stool occult blood test is positive before randomization;
23. History of drug abuse or positive urine drug screening at screening/baseline visit;
